From: TheDBP <TheDBP@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 14:14:43 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] SettingsProvider: seed FONT_SCALE from a device resource

ether ships the panel at 320 dpi, which reports this 1080x1920 screen as 540 dp wide. That is the
room dense layouts need, but it leaves text physically small on 5.2 inches, so the device wants the
font one notch up out of the box.

AOSP has no default for Settings.System.FONT_SCALE: every reader passes 1.0f and nothing seeds the
database, so there is no resource to overlay and no way to ship a different starting point without
this. Read it through loadFractionSetting with base 1, so the value lives in the device overlay
(def_font_scale, 115%) and this carries no device-specific number.
---
 .../src/com/android/providers/settings/DatabaseHelper.java | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/packages/SettingsProvider/src/com/android/providers/settings/DatabaseHelper.java b/packages/SettingsProvider/src/com/android/providers/settings/DatabaseHelper.java
index 62fff96c57ad..0c39c3e15519 100644
--- a/packages/SettingsProvider/src/com/android/providers/settings/DatabaseHelper.java
+++ b/packages/SettingsProvider/src/com/android/providers/settings/DatabaseHelper.java
@@ -2263,6 +2263,13 @@ class DatabaseHelper extends SQLiteOpenHelper {
             loadBooleanSetting(stmt, Settings.System.SCREEN_BRIGHTNESS_MODE,
                     R.bool.def_screen_brightness_automatic_mode);
 
+            // ether: text one notch up to compensate for shipping the panel at 320 dpi. The
+            // resource lives in the device overlay, so this reads whatever that sets rather than
+            // hardcoding a scale here. Base 1, so 115% becomes 1.15 -- the second step of the
+            // SettingsLib ladder, which keeps it a normal selection in Settings.
+            loadFractionSetting(stmt, Settings.System.FONT_SCALE,
+                    R.fraction.def_font_scale, 1);
+
             loadBooleanSetting(stmt, Settings.System.ACCELEROMETER_ROTATION,
                     R.bool.def_accelerometer_rotation);
 
